# <%= name %>

`<%= name %>` is an AWS CDK app. `<%= className %>` is empty. Add constructs in `src/constructs` and compose them from `src/stacks`.

## Commands

From the repository root:

```bash
bunx nx run <%= name %>:lint
bunx nx run <%= name %>:typecheck
bunx nx run <%= name %>:test
bunx nx run <%= name %>:build
bunx nx run <%= name %>:synth
bunx nx run <%= name %>:deploy
```

`deploy` uses the AWS account and region in your environment. This repo does not store account ids.

## Layout

`src/functions` is pure logic. `src/lambdas` is the handler. `src/constructs` is CDK. `src/stacks` composes constructs. Imports go in that direction only.

## Gotchas

`cdk synth` does not need AWS credentials while the stack stays environment-agnostic. ESLint rejects imports that skip a layer, and imports of another app.
